  "question": {
    "text": "An initially parallel cylindrical beam travels in a medium of refractive index $\\mu(I)=\\mu_0+\\mu_2 I$, where $\\mu_0$ and $\\mu_2$ are positive constants and $\\mathrm{I}$ is the intensity of the light beam. The intensity of the beam is decreasing with increasing radius.\nThe initial shape of the wave front of the beam is",
    "image": null
